{"availability":"available","full":"ValentinTorassa/VT-Agent-Firewall","name":"VT-Agent-Firewall","description":"Local security gateway between an AI agent and its tools (fs, shell, network, MCP): default-deny policy engine, human approval, append-only audit log. Tested against indirect prompt injection trying to exfiltrate a fake .env to 127.0.0.1. Python stdlib only, 21 acceptance tests. Not production-ready - a security lab.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":7,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-28T02:06:29Z","updated":"2026-10-04T12:02:53Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://valentorassa.com/charlas/hacking-day-2026","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:55.053Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:55.053Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:55.053Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T08:18:55.053Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2106049012470051274","postId":"2106049012470051274","postedAt":"2026-10-02T15:49:47.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T08:18:55.053Z","stars":7,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fail-closed gateway between an AI agent and its tools. The agent never calls open, subprocess or the network directly: every action is a request that goes through the same pipeline, and anything the pipeline cannot vouch for is denied.","Three possible decisions: allow, block, requireapproval. If a parser fails or the audit store is unavailable, the answer is block: the gateway would rather stop than act unaudited.","Status: alpha (0.2.0). Standard library only, Python 3.11+. Built as the reference implementation for the talk \"Dónde se rompe OAuth cuando el que llama es un agente\" (OWASP Village, Ekoparty 2026). Not production-ready; see Limitations."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ValentinTorassa/VT-Agent-Firewall/blob/main/README.md",